EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# When testing on a physical device (Expo Go / a dev build) over the LAN,
# localhost will not work - set this to your computer's current LAN IP
# instead, e.g.:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.32:4000
#
# Known recurring failure mode: on networks using DHCP, your Mac's LAN IP
# can change (router reassigns it) whenever your machine reconnects to
# Wi-Fi/wakes from sleep/the router restarts. When that happens, this file
# goes stale and every request from the app fails with a raw network error
# ("fetch failed: Could not connect to the server" or similar) even though
# the backend is running fine - the app is just pointed at an IP that is no
# longer yours. The app surfaces a friendlier message for this case now
# (see app/src/services/apiRequest.ts's isNetworkError), but it still needs
# a correct IP in this file to actually reach the server.
#
# To fix it quickly:
#   1. ipconfig getifaddr en0        (prints your Mac's current LAN IP)
#   2. Update EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL above to that IP (keep the :4000 port)
#   3. Restart the Expo dev server so it picks up the change (`expo start`
#      re-reads .env on startup, not on hot reload)
#
# The durable fix is a static DHCP lease/IP reservation for this Mac in
# your router's settings, so the IP stops drifting at all - that's a
# router configuration change outside this codebase, not something this
# app can fix for you.
